            <!-- Section 6: Install Docker -->
            <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 rounded-4 mb-4 border-start border-4 border-primary section-card">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3"><span class="section-num">6</span> 💻 How to Install Docker (Step by Step)</h3>
                    <p>Follow these steps exactly. Do not skip any.</p>

                    <h5 class="mt-4 mb-2">🪟 Windows</h5>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Go to <a href="https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop" target="_blank">docker.com/products/docker-desktop</a>.</li>
                        <li>Click <strong>Download for Windows</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Run the installer (<code>Docker Desktop Installer.exe</code>).</li>
                        <li>During setup, keep <strong>"Use WSL 2"</strong> checked (recommended).</li>
                        <li>Click <strong>Ok</strong> and wait for install to finish.</li>
                        <li>Restart your computer when asked.</li>
                        <li>Open <strong>Docker Desktop</strong> from the Start Menu.</li>
                        <li>Accept the terms. Wait for the whale icon 🐳 in the taskbar.</li>
                        <li>Done. Docker is running.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <h5 class="mt-4 mb-2">🍎 macOS</h5>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Download <strong>Docker Desktop for Mac</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Choose <em>Apple Silicon</em> or <em>Intel</em> based on your Mac.</li>
                        <li>Open the <code>.dmg</code> file.</li>
                        <li>Drag the Docker icon into <strong>Applications</strong>.</li>
                        <li>Open Docker from Applications.</li>
                        <li>Accept the terms and give permission.</li>
                        <li>Wait for the whale icon 🐳 in the menu bar.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <h5 class="mt-4 mb-2">🐧 Linux (Ubuntu)</h5>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Open a terminal.</li>
                        <li>Run: <code>sudo apt update</code></li>
                        <li>Run: <code>sudo apt install docker.io -y</code></li>
                        <li>Run: <code>sudo systemctl start docker</code></li>
                        <li>Run: <code>sudo systemctl enable docker</code></li>
                        <li>To run docker without sudo: <code>sudo usermod -aG docker $USER</code></li>
                        <li>Log out and log back in.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <div class="alert alert-success border-0 bg-success bg-opacity-10 mt-3">
                        <strong>✅ Verify the installation:</strong><br />
                        Open a terminal and run: <code>docker --version</code><br />
                        You should see something like <code>Docker version 24.0.0</code>.
                        If you do, you are ready!
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- JOKE 3 -->
            <div class="joke-card">
                <div class="joke-emoji">🤣</div>
                <div class="joke-body">
                    <strong>DevOps Joke #3:</strong>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        Docker walked into a bar and asked for a drink.
